course: dictionary
lesson: 2223
title: A cove, a bay, or a man?
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A cove is a small, sheltered bay where the land curves round the water, so the sea is calmer inside it. «The fishing boats rested in a quiet cove, safe from the big waves.» The clues sheltered and curves tell you a cove is a little bay, not an open sea.
explain: Waves can make coves. Where waves wear away soft rock behind harder rock, a cove can form, like Lulworth Cove in England. «In 1788 the First Fleet brought convicts and soldiers to Sydney Cove.» Here cove is a place name, a bay on the coast.
explain: Cove also has an old slang meaning in the UK and Australia: a man or fellow. «He is a strange cove, always whistling to himself.» The words around it tell you it is a person, not a place. Always check which meaning fits the sentence.
fact: A cove is a small, sheltered bay on a coastline.
fact: «Sheltered» means protected from the wind and the waves.
fact: Lulworth Cove in England was shaped when waves wore away soft rock behind harder rock.
fact: «Cove» in old slang, used in the UK and Australia, means a man or fellow, as in «a strange cove».
fact: In adventure stories, smugglers and pirates often use coves as hiding places.
exercise: «The ship sailed into the sheltered cove to hide from the storm.» What is a cove? | A tall mountain peak | *A small, sheltered bay on the coast | A ship's sail | A busy city street
exercise: «He is a strange cove, always whistling to himself.» In this sentence, what does cove mean? | A bay of calm water | A sheltered rock | *A man or fellow | A small boat
exercise: Why are coves good hiding places for smugglers in adventure stories? | Because they are high up on mountains | Because they are always full of people | *Because they are sheltered and out of sight | Because they are always dry
test: «In 1788 eleven ships brought convicts and soldiers to Sydney Cove.» What kind of place is Sydney Cove? | A castle on a hill | *A bay on the coast where ships could sail in | A large desert inland | A forest of tall trees
test: «The First Fleet of eleven ships brought convicts to Sydney Cove.» What was the First Fleet? | *A group of eleven ships | A school of fish | A team of footballers | A flock of birds
exam: What is the best way to work out a new word like cove? | Ask no one and never check a dictionary | Guess a meaning without reading the sentence | *Read the words around it, then swap in your meaning to check it fits the sentence | Skip the whole text and never come back to it
